# S10.2 (PLAN.md, acceptance scenarios): the k14 design point on paper.
# Per BK=16 tile each warp issues 4x4 output tiles x 2 mma.sync.m16n8k16
# = 32 MMAs = 32 * 128 = 4096 f16 tensor FLOPs per lane and no
# cuda-core FLOPs; the tile's A and B panels arrive by four 16-byte
# cp.async per thread = 64 global bytes (an upper bound: the prefetch is
# guarded by `tile + 2 < num_k_tiles`), so AI(global) = 64. Fragments
# come from shared via ldmatrix: 4 x4 (16 B) + 8 x2 (8 B) = 128 B per
# lane. K / 16 trips through nvcc's signed-divide sequence; the
# epilogue loop runs 4. On the A100 table 64 flop/B is below the f16
# tensor peak ratio (312 TFLOPS / 1555 GB/s = 200.6 flop/B). The tile
# issues 101 instructions per lane per iteration, 48 of them workload:
# 32 mma, 12 ldmatrix, 4 cp.async.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/k14/k14.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k14/k14.sm_80.ptx --json | %check-report "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z18hgemm_ldmatrix_mmaILi128ELi128ELi16ELi64ELi64ELi128ELi8ELi8EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // shared memory 20,992 B/CTA | per thread: flops f32 <= 384; tensor flops f16 (4096·(param_2 / 16)); global load <= (64·(param_2 / 16) + 384) B, store <= 512 B; shared load (128·(param_2 / 16)) B, store <= (64·(param_2 / 16) + 128) B; local load <= 960 B, store <= 1,024 B; param load 44 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_4: // loop: trips param_2 / 16 | under line 267 | exec (param_2 / 16)/thread{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_12: // loop: trips 4 | exec 4/thread{{$}}
